  "section_notes": "The final text keeps per-model test results away from the general public while giving them to purchasers and regulators, and it removes any automatic sales ban above the 5% S2 test limit and the 8/100k S5 trigger, which favours Northwind's flagship (6.2% failure rate) and Halcyon's flagship (9.9 incidents) respectively. The remote shut-off retrofit runs 72 months, which benefits Northwind given its 38% existing shut-off coverage. S1 excludes minor overheating events that do not require service or shutdown, and the rules set no numeric sales stop above the S2 limit, so the weakest parameters are S1 scope, S2 enforcement and S5 corrective-action flexibility."
